{"nodes": [{"id": "_agents_skills_revenue_centric_design_references_metrics_and_experimentation_metrics__experimentation___business_math", "label": "Metrics, Experimentation & Business Math", "file_type": "document", "source_file": ".agents/skills/revenue-centric-design/references/metrics-and-experimentation.md", "source_location": "document", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "_agents_skills_revenue_centric_design_references_metrics_and_experimentation_duolingo_s_lesson__optimize_the_metric_that_moves_dau__not_the_borrowed_mechanic", "label": "Duolingo's lesson: optimize the metric that moves DAU, not the borrowed mechanic", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".agents/skills/revenue-centric-design/references/metrics-and-experimentation.md", "source_location": "section: Duolingo's lesson: optimize the metric that moves DAU, not the borrowed mechanic", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Duolingo copied game mechanics twice and failed both (a Gardenscapes moves-counter: neutral; a referral program copied from Uber: +3% because the reward excluded the best users). They stopped picking mechanics and modeled which number to move: bucketing users by engagement and simulating +2%/quarter for 3 years, CURR (current-user retention rate) had ~5x the impact of the next-best metric. Then gamification worked: CURR +21% over 4 years, daily churn of best users \u221240%+, DAU \u00d74.5. Leaderboards alone +17% total learning time and tripled highly-engaged learners \u2014 because they switched to competing with users of *similar prior-week engagement* (auto opt-in = default effect, no extra tasks)."}, {"id": "_agents_skills_revenue_centric_design_references_metrics_and_experimentation_don_t_mistake_signups_for_traction", "label": "Don't mistake signups for traction", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".agents/skills/revenue-centric-design/references/metrics-and-experimentation.md", "source_location": "section: Don't mistake signups for traction", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Signups are the cheapest action a user takes, so they measure curiosity, not value \u2014 especially in freemium. Real growth is whether people come back and do the action that delivers value."}, {"id": "_agents_skills_revenue_centric_design_references_metrics_and_experimentation_don_t_bet_your_product_on_an_underpowered_a_b_test", "label": "Don't bet your product on an underpowered A/B test", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".agents/skills/revenue-centric-design/references/metrics-and-experimentation.md", "source_location": "section: Don't bet your product on an underpowered A/B test", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Most A/B tests in small SaaS lack the volume to prove anything, yet founders swap the whole product on the result. Testing without enough sample to conclude is the trap."}, {"id": "_agents_skills_revenue_centric_design_references_metrics_and_experimentation_celebrate_signal_quality__not_list_size", "label": "Celebrate signal quality, not list size", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".agents/skills/revenue-centric-design/references/metrics-and-experimentation.md", "source_location": "section: Celebrate signal quality, not list size", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A waitlist exists to validate that a pain is one people pay to solve \u2014 not to sell. Absolute size is a vanity metric; conversion-weighted quality is the real signal."}, {"id": "_agents_skills_revenue_centric_design_references_metrics_and_experimentation_translate_churn_points_into_ltv__not_percentages", "label": "Translate churn points into LTV, not percentages", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".agents/skills/revenue-centric-design/references/metrics-and-experimentation.md", "source_location": "section: Translate churn points into LTV, not percentages", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Most people watch churn %, but few compute what each point costs in accumulated LTV over 12 months. Cutting churn is a cash lever that needs no price hike or new acquisition."}, {"id": "_agents_skills_revenue_centric_design_references_metrics_and_experimentation_nine_product_metrics__each_telling_one_thing", "label": "Nine product metrics, each telling one thing", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".agents/skills/revenue-centric-design/references/metrics-and-experimentation.md", "source_location": "section: Nine product metrics, each telling one thing", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "ARR = size (not necessarily health). Burn rate = risk (time until death). CAC = efficiency (but obsessing over lowering it can worsen conversion with a less-qualified cohort). DAU/MAU = engagement (<20% = bad sign). LTV = product (does the customer see value?). Churn = fit (user doesn't understand or see value \u2192 cancels). NRR = real growth (>100% = good). Gross margin = model (<70% in SaaS = problem, except AI wrappers). Runway = survival (<12 months = danger). Metrics are like a blood panel \u2014 one bad reading is critical, but all-good is real health."}, {"id": "_agents_skills_revenue_centric_design_references_metrics_and_experimentation__richardrx___2026_07_27", "label": "@richardrx \u00b7 2026-07-27", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".agents/skills/revenue-centric-design/references/metrics-and-experimentation.md", "source_location": "link: @richardrx \u00b7 2026-07-27", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "reference_url": "https://x.com/richardrx/status/2081714430811730162"}, {"id": "_agents_skills_revenue_centric_design_references_metrics_and_experimentation__richardrx___2026_06_11"